smolagents.utils.AgentGenerationError: Error in generating model output:

litellm.NotFoundError: NotFoundError: OpenrouterException - {"error":{"message":"No endpoints found for anthropic/claude-3.5-sonnet.","code":404},"user_id":"user_3Clh8pj76aUpYjhARZhpw4aGyS1"}

That 404 Not Found error from OpenRouter is usually due to a tiny typo in the model identifier string.

In your log, it says: No endpoints found for anthropic/claude-3.5-sonnet.
Notice the decimal point: 3.5. In OpenRouter's API, the model ID uses a hyphen for the version number instead of a dot.

The Fix
Update your .env file (or the default value in your code) to use the correct slug.

Change this:
openrouter/anthropic/claude-3.5-sonnet

To this:
openrouter/anthropic/claude-3-5-sonnet (use a hyphen - instead of a dot .)

Where to apply it
Look at this section in your main.py and ensure the MODEL_ID or the default string is exactly as follows:

Python
# Check your .env file first, but you can also fix the fallback here:
MODEL_ID = os.getenv("MODEL_ID", "openrouter/anthropic/claude-3-5-sonnet")
Why this happens
OpenRouter follows a specific naming convention for their model slugs. If you use a version number like 3.5, their router doesn't recognize the path and throws a 404 because, technically, that specific URL endpoint doesn't exist on their server.

Commonly used correct slugs:

openrouter/anthropic/claude-3-5-sonnet

openrouter/anthropic/claude-3-5-sonnet:beta

openrouter/google/gemini-2.0-flash-001 (Note: Google models sometimes do use dots, so it depends on the provider!)

Try that change and restart your server—it should clear right up!

